{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 3,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.046,
            0.364,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.087,
            0.846,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": "• We then multiplied the result by the numerator of the multiplier, that is 2, to get ${ \\frac { 6 } { 5 } } .$ Multiplier Multiplicand"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.146,
            0.523,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": "Thus, whenever we need to multiply a fraction and a whole number, we follow the steps above."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.21,
            0.524,
            0.288
          ],
          "content": "**Example 1:** A farmer had 5 grandchildren. She distributed $\\frac { 2 } { 3 }$ acre of land to each of her grandchildren."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.528,
            0.116,
            0.839,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.295,
            0.714,
            0.316
          ],
          "content": "How much land in all did she give to her grandchildren?"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.359,
            0.321,
            0.638,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "5 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{10}{3}.",
          "image_source": "images/page_3_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.376,
            0.847,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": "? **Example 2:** 1 hour of internet time costs ₹8. How much will 1 $\\frac{1}{4}$ hours of internet time cost?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.44,
            0.704,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": "1 $\\frac { 1 } { 4 }$ hours is $\\frac { 5 } { 4 }$ hours (converting from a mixed fraction)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.477,
            0.536,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": "Cost of $\\frac { 5 } { 4 }$ hour of internet time $\\begin{aligned}&=\\frac{5}{4} \\times 8 \\\\&= 5 \\times \\frac{8}{4} \\\\&= 5 \\times 2 \\\\&= 10.\\end{aligned}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.602,
            0.564,
            0.635
          ],
          "content": "It costs ₹10 for $1 { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } }$ hours of internet time."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.641,
            0.293,
            0.665
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.672,
            0.848,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": "1. Tenzin drinks $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ glass of milk every day. How many glasses of milk does he drink in a week? How many glasses of milk did he drink in the month of January?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.748,
            0.848,
            0.806
          ],
          "content": "2. A team of workers can make 1 km of a water canal in 8 days. So, in one day, the team can make \\_\\_\\_ km of the water canal. If they work 5 days a week, they can make \\_\\_\\_ km of the water canal in a week."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.809,
            0.849,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": "3. Manju and two of her neighbours buy 5 litres of oil every week and share it equally among the 3 families. How much oil does each family get in a week? How much oil will one family get in 4 weeks?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.87,
            0.848,
            0.923
          ],
          "content": "4. Safia saw the Moon setting on Monday at 10 pm. Her mother, who is a scientist, told her that every day the Moon sets $\\frac{5}{6}$ hour later than"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.938,
            0.193,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": "176"
        },
